WEBVTT

00:00:01.220 --> 00:00:04.310
Three traps catch Grade 10s every year.

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:05.550
Here they are.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:07.270
One, no direction.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.070
Momentum change in momentum, impulse and force all need a direction.

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:16.330
Or a sign with your positive direction stated.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:18.870
Two, the bounce.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:23.050
The ball on your card goes in at 5 metres per second.

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:25.050
It comes back at 3.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.750
The two velocities have opposite signs.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:30.090
Final minus initial.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:34.350
Negative 3, take away 5, not 3, take away 5.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:38.390
The examiners wrote this about matric candidates.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:44.550
The change in direction of the ball was often disregarded in the mathematics.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:49.010
So draw a sketch and choose a positive direction.

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:51.350
Three, the airbag.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:54.010
The change in momentum does not get smaller.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:56.070
The time gets longer.

00:00:56.380 --> 00:00:58.070
So the force gets smaller.

00:00:59.120 --> 00:00:59.850
And a bonus.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:01.470
Milliseconds.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:05.630
20 milliseconds is 0,02 seconds.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:08.370
Convert before you divide.

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:12.250
Now try the twin on the card.

